## The case's authored text -- there is NONE

Measured from `ck.db` `zephyr_cases` at triage: `has_objective = 0`, and the single "step" is an
**empty placeholder** (`[{"description": "", "testData": "", "expected": ""}]`).

**There is not one word of authored objective, procedure, test data or expected result for this
case beyond its title.** The steps below were designed by this tester from the title, the X960
TPS, `platforms/x960.md` and the DUT's own CLI surface.

### The requirement this case is graded against

**X960 TPS row 235 "Management ACLs" = Yes**, and the requirement statement the row implements,
**TPS 6.1.1**, verbatim:

> *"Access filter for management I/F, which denies all packets addressed to the management I/F
> other than those packets that come from user specified network(s) or host(s). Also TCP/UDP
> port number of all services such as telnet, SNMP, ICMP and etc. is configurable."*

That is **two** separate statements, and this case proves both:
- **(A)** an access filter that denies traffic to the management interface except from
  specified hosts;
- **(B)** the TCP/UDP port number of a management service is configurable.

### The grading rules this case is built on

1. 🔴 **`platforms/x960.md` section 5: hardware ACLs implicitly PERMIT what no rule denies;
   software/standard ACLs implicitly DENY.** Opposite defaults. Grading the wrong default round
   is the easiest false pass available here, so every limb below states which kind of list it
   uses and what its implicit action is.
2. 🔴 **`platforms/x960.md` section 5 and 7F.2: this platform reports features Enabled while the
   dataplane does nothing.** `show mirror` passed five mirroring cases that copied no frames;
   `show telnet` read `Enabled` while IPv4 TCP/23 was refused. **So every verdict below is taken
   from the wire.** Every `show` quoted is corroboration, never evidence.
3. 🔴 **A refused SERVICE and a rejected CREDENTIAL look completely different on the wire, and
   only one of them is a refusal** (group A's T33380 finding, `platforms/x960.md` section 7F.10).
   This case never grades a block on a login verdict at all: it counts packets and reads TCP
   flags, where **SYN-ACK = open, RST = refused by the service, and nothing back = silently
   dropped by a filter**. Those are three different answers and a management-ACL case is
   precisely that three-way discrimination.
4. 🔴 **STANDING-ORDERS section 7: the exact frame plus a control flow that must NOT match, both
   counted, in the same run.** Every leg below carries at least one control.

