### Item 10 in detail -- every command was read off the platform BEFORE it was sent

This is the gate that matters most here, because the obvious design for a "Management ACL"
case does not exist on this platform. All of the following were measured with `qmark.py`, which
types `<prefix> ?` with **no carriage return**, prints the completions and clears the line with
Ctrl-U, after a self-test proving nothing is executed (memory
`never-send-cli-help-through-a-cr-driver` -- `<cmd> ?` through a CR driver EXECUTES the
command).

🔴 **The Cisco-style design is impossible here, and this is a first-class result of the case.**

```
awplus(config-line)#acc ?            [inside `line vty 0 7`]
  login  Set accounting method list for login session

awplus(config-line)#access-class ?
% Unrecognized command

awplus(config)#ip access-list ?
% Unrecognized command

awplus(config)#ip access ?
% Unrecognized command
```

**There is no `access-class` under `line vty` on this platform** -- the only `acc...` completion
offered is `accounting`-related `login`. **And there is no `ip access-list` in global config at
all.** A test designed from the Cisco pattern would have failed at its first command and
measured nothing. (Note `platforms/x960.md` section 5 records the ACL guide saying "Standard
lists still bind to `vty access-class`" -- **that generic AW+ statement does not hold on this
build**, which is itself worth recording.)

